IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`
IMPORT `aia-scope`

-- P9-art-99: Chapter XII "Penalties": Article 99 "Penalties" (consolidated text of 27.7.2026).
-- The Omnibus replaced paragraph 1 (the SMCs added to the interests Member States take into account), inserted point (da) of
-- paragraph 4 (Article 25(2) and (4)) and inserted paragraph 6a (the lower limit for SMCs). Each text that changed is encoded
-- as a function for each version (as-enacted quotes are `src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:N`) and a dispatcher.
-- Group `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` (2 August 2025). A fine for non-compliance with a substantive
-- obligation is also gated on the group of the obligation: Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 (points (a) to (e), (da)) with
-- Article 111(2)'s saving, and General (point (g), Article 50). Money is a NUMBER of euros; a turnover is the total worldwide
-- annual turnover for the preceding financial year, stated by the caller.
-- Split site (i) (an unmet element of an infringement): each "Non-compliance with X shall be subject to administrative fines"
-- sentence answers NOTHING when the non-compliance is not established, because the sentence has no "where", "if" or "only"
-- (the subject of the sentence is the non-compliance, a scope limit with no "only": ruling (c) of 2026-11-05). Forks F-99-3, F-99-4, F-99-5.
-- The Member States are officials: no seat. What the Article means to an operator is asked in the seat modules.

§ `Seam S14: the reference this Article gives to Article 2(2)`

-- Article 2(2): for a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in
-- Section B of Annex I, "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply". The keel asks of a provision by its Article
-- number, letter and paragraph; paragraph 0 means the whole Article.

`Art 99 reference to the provision` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
    number IS 99
    letter IS ""
    paragraph IS 0

§ `Article 99: the parties, the acts, the infringements and the factors`

DECLARE `Art 99 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 99 the Member State`

DECLARE `Art 99 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 99(1) lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures`
    `Art 99(1) take into account the interests and economic viability of the enterprise when imposing penalties`
    `Art 99(2) notify the Commission of the rules on penalties and of other enforcement measures`
    `Art 99(8) lay down rules on to what extent administrative fines may be imposed on public authorities and bodies established in the Member State`
    `Art 99(11) report to the Commission about the administrative fines issued during the year and about any related litigation or judicial proceedings`

-- The infringements that paragraphs 3, 4 and 5 name. Point (da) exists as amended only.
DECLARE `Art 99 infringement` IS ONE OF
    `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5`
    `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16`
    `Art 99(4)(b) non-compliance with the obligations of authorised representatives pursuant to Article 22`
    `Art 99(4)(c) non-compliance with the obligations of importers pursuant to Article 23`
    `Art 99(4)(d) non-compliance with the obligations of distributors pursuant to Article 24`
    `Art 99(4)(da) non-compliance with the obligations of providers and operators pursuant to Article 25(2) and (4)`
    `Art 99(4)(e) non-compliance with the obligations of deployers pursuant to Article 26`
    `Art 99(4)(f) non-compliance with the requirements and obligations of notified bodies pursuant to Article 31, Article 33(1), (3) and (4) or Article 34`
    `Art 99(4)(g) non-compliance with the transparency obligations for providers and deployers pursuant to Article 50`
    `Art 99(5) the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request`
    `Art 99 another infringement`

-- The factors of paragraph 7 (a) to (j).
DECLARE `Art 99(7) factor` IS ONE OF
    `Art 99(7)(a) the nature, gravity and duration of the infringement and of its consequences, taking into account the purpose of the AI system, as well as, where appropriate, the number of affected persons and the level of damage suffered by them`
    `Art 99(7)(b) whether administrative fines have already been applied by other market surveillance authorities to the same operator for the same infringement`
    `Art 99(7)(c) whether administrative fines have already been applied by other authorities to the same operator for infringements of other Union or national law, when such infringements result from the same activity or omission`
    `Art 99(7)(d) the size, the annual turnover and market share of the operator committing the infringement`
    `Art 99(7)(e) any other aggravating or mitigating factor applicable to the circumstances of the case`
    `Art 99(7)(f) the degree of cooperation with the national competent authorities, in order to remedy the infringement and mitigate the possible adverse effects of the infringement`
    `Art 99(7)(g) the degree of responsibility of the operator taking into account the technical and organisational measures implemented by it`
    `Art 99(7)(h) the manner in which the infringement became known to the national competent authorities, in particular whether, and if so to what extent, the operator notified the infringement`
    `Art 99(7)(i) the intentional or negligent character of the infringement`
    `Art 99(7)(j) any action taken by the operator to mitigate the harm suffered by the affected persons`
    `Art 99(7) another factor`

§ `Article 99(1): the Member States' rules on penalties`

-- src:1473 | 1. In accordance with the terms and conditions laid down in this Regulation, Member States shall lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures, which may also include administrative fines, warnings and non-monetary measures, applicable to any infringement of this Regulation by operators, and shall take all measures necessary to ensure that they are properly and effectively implemented, thereby taking into account the guidelines issued by the Commission pursuant to Article 96. The penalties provided for shall be effective, proportionate and dissuasive. The Member States shall take into account the interests of SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs, and their economic viability when imposing penalties.
@ref Art 99(1) (src:1473)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 99(1) the Member States must lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures` MEANS
    IF `Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed

@ref Art 99(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 99 party` `Art 99 act`
`Art 99(1) the duty of the Member States to lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 99(1) the Member States must lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures` `the date asked`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 99 the Member State`
        MUST `Art 99(1) lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

@ref Art 99(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the penalties provided for are effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalties provided for are proportionate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalties provided for are dissuasive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 99(1) the penalties provided for are effective, proportionate and dissuasive` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is required
    ELSE IF       `the penalties provided for are effective`
              AND `the penalties provided for are proportionate`
              AND `the penalties provided for are dissuasive`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The penalties provided for shall be effective, proportionate and dissuasive" (a requirement of manner: not met means the requirement is not met)

-- The interests the Member States take into account when imposing penalties: SMEs including start-ups (and, as amended, SMCs) and their economic viability.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2009 | 1. In accordance with the terms and conditions laid down in this Regulation, Member States shall lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures, which may also include warnings and non-monetary measures, applicable to infringements of this Regulation by operators, and shall take all measures necessary to ensure that they are properly and effectively implemented, thereby taking into account the guidelines issued by the Commission pursuant to Article 96. The penalties provided for shall be effective, proportionate and dissuasive. They shall take into account the interests of SMEs, including start-ups, and their economic viability.
@ref Art 99(1) as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2009)
GIVEN `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 99(1) as enacted the interests and economic viability of the enterprise must be taken into account` MEANS
    IF `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): VERSION as enacted. The sentence is about "the interests of SMEs, including start-ups, and their economic viability"; for another enterprise it is silent

-- src:1473 | 1. In accordance with the terms and conditions laid down in this Regulation, Member States shall lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures, which may also include administrative fines, warnings and non-monetary measures, applicable to any infringement of this Regulation by operators, and shall take all measures necessary to ensure that they are properly and effectively implemented, thereby taking into account the guidelines issued by the Commission pursuant to Article 96. The penalties provided for shall be effective, proportionate and dissuasive. The Member States shall take into account the interests of SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs, and their economic viability when imposing penalties.
@ref Art 99(1) as amended (src:1473)
GIVEN `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enterprise is an SMC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 99(1) as amended the interests and economic viability of the enterprise must be taken into account` MEANS
    IF `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` OR `the enterprise is an SMC`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): VERSION as amended. The sentence is about "the interests of SMEs, including start-ups, and SMCs, and their economic viability"; for another enterprise it is silent

@ref Art 99(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enterprise is an SMC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 99(1) the Member States must take into account the interests and economic viability of the enterprise when imposing penalties` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 99(1) as enacted the interests and economic viability of the enterprise must be taken into account` `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up`  -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 99(1) as amended the interests and economic viability of the enterprise must be taken into account` `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` `the enterprise is an SMC`  -- VERSION as amended

@ref Art 99(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enterprise is an SMC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 99 party` `Art 99 act`
`Art 99(1) the duty of the Member States to take into account the interests and economic viability of the enterprise` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 99(1) the Member States must take into account the interests and economic viability of the enterprise when imposing penalties` `the date asked` `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up` `the enterprise is an SMC`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 99 the Member State`
        MUST `Art 99(1) take into account the interests and economic viability of the enterprise when imposing penalties`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 99(2): the notification of the rules, by the date of entry into application`

-- "without delay and at the latest by the date of entry into application": the date of application of the group of Chapter XII (2 August 2025).
-- The caller states the day from which the time is counted: the day the duty began (the entry into force of the Regulation, 1 August 2024).
-- src:1475 | 2. The Member States shall, without delay and at the latest by the date of entry into application, notify the Commission of the rules on penalties and of other enforcement measures referred to in paragraph 1, and shall notify it, without delay, of any subsequent amendment to them.
@ref Art 99(2) (src:1475)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the day from which the time is counted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 99 party` `Art 99 act`
`Art 99(2) the duty of the Member State to notify the Commission of the rules on penalties` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Article 113 gives this provision its date of application (fork F-99-2)
    ELSE PARTY `Art 99 the Member State`
         MUST `Art 99(2) notify the Commission of the rules on penalties and of other enforcement measures`
         WITHIN (Day (`Art 113(b) the group of Chapter III Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Article 78 applies from`)) MINUS (Day `the day from which the time is counted`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 99 the Member State` BECAUSE "the rules on penalties and the other enforcement measures were not notified to the Commission by the date of entry into application"

§ `Article 99(3), (4) and (5): the infringements that are subject to administrative fines`

-- args: date asked, the AI system, the infringement, the non-compliance (or the supply) is established.
-- Article 5 and the notified bodies' obligations and the supply of information are gated by the group of this Article alone; points (a) to (e)
-- and (da) also by the group Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 for the AI system (Article 111(2)); point (g) also by the group General.
-- Point (da) exists as amended only: the as-enacted list is the function below, the as-amended list the next.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2013 | (a)
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2014 | obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2015 | (b)
