§ `Article 99(3), (4), (5), (6) and (6a): the ceilings of the fines`

-- Paragraph 3: EUR 35 000 000 or 7 %; paragraph 4: EUR 15 000 000 or 3 %; paragraph 5: EUR 7 500 000 or 1 %. "if the offender is an
-- undertaking, up to [the percentage] of its total worldwide annual turnover for the preceding financial year, whichever is higher".
-- Paragraph 6: SMEs including start-ups: "whichever thereof is lower"; paragraph 6a (as amended): SMCs, for paragraphs 4 and 5 only.
@ref Art 99(3), (4) and (5)
GIVEN `the infringement` IS AN `Art 99 infringement`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Art 99 the amount in euros of the ceiling` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the infringement`
    WHEN `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` THEN JUST 35000000
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` THEN JUST 15000000
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(b) non-compliance with the obligations of authorised representatives pursuant to Article 22` THEN JUST 15000000
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(c) non-compliance with the obligations of importers pursuant to Article 23` THEN JUST 15000000
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(d) non-compliance with the obligations of distributors pursuant to Article 24` THEN JUST 15000000
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(da) non-compliance with the obligations of providers and operators pursuant to Article 25(2) and (4)` THEN JUST 15000000
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(e) non-compliance with the obligations of deployers pursuant to Article 26` THEN JUST 15000000
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(f) non-compliance with the requirements and obligations of notified bodies pursuant to Article 31, Article 33(1), (3) and (4) or Article 34` THEN JUST 15000000
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(g) non-compliance with the transparency obligations for providers and deployers pursuant to Article 50` THEN JUST 15000000
    WHEN `Art 99(5) the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request` THEN JUST 7500000
    WHEN `Art 99 another infringement` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no paragraph states a ceiling for it

@ref Art 99(3), (4) and (5)
GIVEN `the infringement` IS AN `Art 99 infringement`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Art 99 the percentage of turnover of the ceiling` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the infringement`
    WHEN `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` THEN JUST 7
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` THEN JUST 3
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(b) non-compliance with the obligations of authorised representatives pursuant to Article 22` THEN JUST 3
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(c) non-compliance with the obligations of importers pursuant to Article 23` THEN JUST 3
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(d) non-compliance with the obligations of distributors pursuant to Article 24` THEN JUST 3
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(da) non-compliance with the obligations of providers and operators pursuant to Article 25(2) and (4)` THEN JUST 3
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(e) non-compliance with the obligations of deployers pursuant to Article 26` THEN JUST 3
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(f) non-compliance with the requirements and obligations of notified bodies pursuant to Article 31, Article 33(1), (3) and (4) or Article 34` THEN JUST 3
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(g) non-compliance with the transparency obligations for providers and deployers pursuant to Article 50` THEN JUST 3
    WHEN `Art 99(5) the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request` THEN JUST 1
    WHEN `Art 99 another infringement` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no paragraph states a ceiling for it

-- The amount, or the percentage of the turnover: the higher (the general rule) or the lower (paragraphs 6 and 6a).
@ref Art 99(3), (4), (5), (6) and (6a)
GIVEN `the infringement` IS AN `Art 99 infringement`
      `the offender is an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` IS A NUMBER
      `the lower of the two limits applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 99 the amount in euros of the ceiling` `the infringement`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no paragraph states a ceiling for the infringement
    WHEN JUST `the amount` THEN
        CONSIDER `Art 99 the percentage of turnover of the ceiling` `the infringement`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no paragraph states a ceiling for the infringement
        WHEN JUST `the percentage` THEN
            IF NOT `the offender is an undertaking`
            THEN JUST `the amount`  -- "or, if the offender is an undertaking, up to [the percentage]": the percentage is for an undertaking only
            ELSE IF `the lower of the two limits applies`
                 THEN JUST (IF `the amount` AT MOST (`the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` TIMES `the percentage` DIVIDED BY 100) THEN `the amount` ELSE (`the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` TIMES `the percentage` DIVIDED BY 100))  -- "whichever thereof is lower"
                 ELSE JUST (IF `the amount` AT LEAST (`the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` TIMES `the percentage` DIVIDED BY 100) THEN `the amount` ELSE (`the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` TIMES `the percentage` DIVIDED BY 100))  -- "whichever is higher"

-- Paragraph 6a covers "each fine referred to in paragraphs 4 and 5": the infringements of those two paragraphs, not Article 5.
@ref Art 99(6a)
GIVEN `the infringement` IS AN `Art 99 infringement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 99(6a) the infringement is one referred to in paragraph 4 or 5` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the infringement`
    WHEN `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(b) non-compliance with the obligations of authorised representatives pursuant to Article 22` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(c) non-compliance with the obligations of importers pursuant to Article 23` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(d) non-compliance with the obligations of distributors pursuant to Article 24` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(da) non-compliance with the obligations of providers and operators pursuant to Article 25(2) and (4)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(e) non-compliance with the obligations of deployers pursuant to Article 26` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(f) non-compliance with the requirements and obligations of notified bodies pursuant to Article 31, Article 33(1), (3) and (4) or Article 34` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Art 99(4)(g) non-compliance with the transparency obligations for providers and deployers pursuant to Article 50` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Art 99(5) the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Art 99 another infringement` THEN FALSE

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2028 | 6. In the case of SMEs, including start-ups, each fine referred to in this Article shall be up to the percentages or amount referred to in paragraphs 3, 4 and 5, whichever thereof is lower.
@ref Art 99(6) as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2028)
GIVEN `the infringement` IS AN `Art 99 infringement`
      `the offender is an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` IS A NUMBER
      `the offender is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Art 99 as enacted the ceiling of the administrative fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 99(4) as enacted the infringement is one that paragraphs 3 to 5 name` `the infringement`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `the infringement` `the offender is an undertaking` `the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` `the offender is an SME, including a start-up`  -- VERSION as enacted: the lower limit applies to SMEs
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text as enacted states no ceiling for the infringement

-- src:1489 | 6. In the case of SMEs, including start-ups, each fine referred to in this Article shall be up to the percentages or amount referred to in paragraphs 3, 4 and 5, whichever thereof is lower.
-- src:1491 | 6a. In the case of SMCs, each fine referred to in paragraphs 4 and 5 shall be up to the percentages or amount referred therein, whichever is lower.
@ref Art 99(6) and (6a) as amended (src:1489-1491)
GIVEN `the infringement` IS AN `Art 99 infringement`
      `the offender is an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` IS A NUMBER
      `the offender is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is an SMC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Art 99 as amended the ceiling of the administrative fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 99(4) as amended the infringement is one that paragraphs 3 to 5 name` `the infringement`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `the infringement` `the offender is an undertaking` `the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` (`the offender is an SME, including a start-up` OR (`the offender is an SMC` AND `Art 99(6a) the infringement is one referred to in paragraph 4 or 5` `the infringement`))  -- VERSION as amended: the lower limit applies to SMEs, and to SMCs for paragraphs 4 and 5
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text as amended states no ceiling for the infringement

@ref Art 99(3), (4), (5), (6) and (6a)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the infringement` IS AN `Art 99 infringement`
      `the offender is an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` IS A NUMBER
      `the offender is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is an SMC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Art 99 the ceiling of the administrative fine` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that no ceiling is stated
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 99 as enacted the ceiling of the administrative fine` `the infringement` `the offender is an undertaking` `the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` `the offender is an SME, including a start-up`  -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 99 as amended the ceiling of the administrative fine` `the infringement` `the offender is an undertaking` `the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` `the offender is an SME, including a start-up` `the offender is an SMC`  -- VERSION as amended

§ `Article 99(7): what the authority takes into account in deciding on a fine and its amount`

-- src:1493 | 7. When deciding whether to impose an administrative fine and when deciding on the amount of the administrative fine in each individual case, all relevant circumstances of the specific situation shall be taken into account and, as appropriate, regard shall be given to the following:
@ref Art 99(7) (src:1493)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the authority is deciding whether to impose an administrative fine or on its amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstance is relevant to the specific situation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 99(7) the authority must take the circumstance into account` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF       `the authority is deciding whether to impose an administrative fine or on its amount`
              AND `the circumstance is relevant to the specific situation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to take into account "all relevant circumstances of the specific situation" "when deciding whether to impose an administrative fine and when deciding on the amount"

-- src:1494 | (a) the nature, gravity and duration of the infringement and of its consequences, taking into account the purpose of the AI system, as well as, where appropriate, the number of affected persons and the level of damage suffered by them;
-- src:1495 | (b) whether administrative fines have already been applied by other market surveillance authorities to the same operator for the same infringement;
-- src:1496 | (c) whether administrative fines have already been applied by other authorities to the same operator for infringements of other Union or national law, when such infringements result from the same activity or omission constituting a relevant infringement of this Regulation;
-- src:1497 | (d) the size, the annual turnover and market share of the operator committing the infringement;
-- src:1498 | (e) any other aggravating or mitigating factor applicable to the circumstances of the case, such as financial benefits gained, or losses avoided, directly or indirectly, from the infringement;
-- src:1499 | (f) the degree of cooperation with the national competent authorities, in order to remedy the infringement and mitigate the possible adverse effects of the infringement;
-- src:1500 | (g) the degree of responsibility of the operator taking into account the technical and organisational measures implemented by it;
-- src:1501 | (h) the manner in which the infringement became known to the national competent authorities, in particular whether, and if so to what extent, the operator notified the infringement;
-- src:1502 | (i) the intentional or negligent character of the infringement;
-- src:1503 | (j) any action taken by the operator to mitigate the harm suffered by the affected persons.
@ref Art 99(7) points (a) to (j) (src:1494-1503)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the authority is deciding whether to impose an administrative fine or on its amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the factor` IS AN `Art 99(7) factor`
      `it is appropriate to have regard to the factor in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 99(7) regard must be given to the factor` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF NOT `the authority is deciding whether to impose an administrative fine or on its amount`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the factors are for "when deciding whether to impose an administrative fine and when deciding on the amount"
         ELSE CONSIDER `the factor`
              WHEN `Art 99(7) another factor` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "regard shall be given to the following" names points (a) to (j); other relevant circumstances are taken into account under the first part of the paragraph
              OTHERWISE
                  IF `it is appropriate to have regard to the factor in the case`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all relevant circumstances ... shall be taken into account and, as appropriate, regard shall be given to the following" (an "as appropriate" gate on a duty that is not met: fork F-99-7)

§ `Article 99(8) to (11): public authorities, courts, safeguards and the annual report`

-- src:1504 | 8. Each Member State shall lay down rules on to what extent administrative fines may be imposed on public authorities and bodies established in that Member State.
@ref Art 99(8) (src:1504)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 99(8) the Member State must lay down rules on to what extent administrative fines may be imposed on public authorities and bodies` MEANS
    IF `Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed

@ref Art 99(8)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 99 party` `Art 99 act`
`Art 99(8) the duty of the Member State to lay down rules on to what extent administrative fines may be imposed on public authorities and bodies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 99(8) the Member State must lay down rules on to what extent administrative fines may be imposed on public authorities and bodies` `the date asked`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 99 the Member State`
        MUST `Art 99(8) lay down rules on to what extent administrative fines may be imposed on public authorities and bodies established in the Member State`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

@ref Art 99(8)
