    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is stated
    ELSE IF       `the body is a public authority or body established in the Member State`
              AND `the rules of the Member State provide for administrative fines on the body to this extent`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Each Member State shall lay down rules on to what extent administrative fines may be imposed on public authorities and bodies": the extent is for the Member State's rules, which are not among the sources

-- src:1505 | 9. Depending on the legal system of the Member States, the rules on administrative fines may be applied in such a manner that the fines are imposed by competent national courts or by other bodies, as applicable in those Member States. The application of such rules in those Member States shall have an equivalent effect.
@ref Art 99(9) (src:1505)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the fines are imposed by a competent national court or by another body, as applicable in the Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
