    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is stated
    ELSE IF `the fines are imposed by a competent national court or by another body, as applicable in the Member State`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- "Depending on the legal system of the Member States": the legal system is the caller's fact
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to impose the fines "by competent national courts or by other bodies, as applicable in those Member States"; for another body it is silent

@ref Art 99(9)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the rules on administrative fines are applied by competent national courts or by other bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application of the rules has an equivalent effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 99(9) the application of the rules has an equivalent effect` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 99 and 100 the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is required
    ELSE IF NOT `the rules on administrative fines are applied by competent national courts or by other bodies`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "the application of such rules in those Member States", the rules applied by courts or other bodies
         ELSE IF `the application of the rules has an equivalent effect`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application of such rules in those Member States shall have an equivalent effect" (a requirement: not met means the requirement is not met)

